WEBVTT

00:01.350 --> 00:03.390
Hey! What's wrong, Tsubasa?

00:03.730 --> 00:05.520
Can't you solve this?

00:07.320 --> 00:12.040
Oh, at this rate, you won't be able to go
to Brazil, even if you win the tournament!

00:12.040 --> 00:14.400
Now, that would be a problem...

00:16.180 --> 00:18.280
Carlos, let's have a little time-out, okay?

00:18.280 --> 00:21.940
No! You can't have time-outs in football!

00:21.940 --> 00:23.290
It's from Wakabayashi!

00:24.080 --> 00:27.270
<i>Are you doing well, Tsubasa?</i>

00:27.270 --> 00:33.300
<i>Ever since I joined this club in Hamburg, I've been practicing daily.</i>

00:33.300 --> 00:37.800
<i>Isn't the National Tournament coming up soon over in Japan?</i>

00:37.800 --> 00:41.810
<i>I'm tired of hearing you boast about your wins.</i>

00:41.810 --> 00:45.080
<i>From now on, only let me know when you lose.</i>

00:45.080 --> 00:47.810
<i>I'm definitely interested in whoever can beat you.</i>

00:48.480 --> 00:51.320
<i>Actually, the reason I'm sending you this e-mail</i>

00:51.320 --> 00:56.920
<i>is because I've run into someone;
a really skilled guy, just about our age.</i>

00:58.870 --> 01:00.360
Wakabayashi!

01:12.490 --> 01:14.050
Mi...

01:14.050 --> 01:16.430
Misaki!

01:16.430 --> 01:17.360
<i>You guessed it.</i>

01:17.360 --> 01:19.970
<i>His name is Taro Misaki.</i>

01:22.230 --> 01:24.940
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:22.230 --> 01:24.940
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:25.850 --> 01:28.520
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:25.850 --> 01:28.520
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:29.440 --> 01:32.150
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:29.440 --> 01:32.150
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:39.030 --> 01:41.870
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

01:39.030 --> 01:41.870
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

01:41.870 --> 01:48.130
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

01:41.870 --> 01:48.130
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

01:48.130 --> 01:54.010
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta na no ni</i>

01:48.130 --> 01:54.010
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

01:54.010 --> 02:00.600
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

01:54.010 --> 02:00.600
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

02:00.600 --> 02:04.600
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

02:00.600 --> 02:04.600
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

02:04.600 --> 02:09.110
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

02:04.600 --> 02:09.110
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

02:09.110 --> 02:14.650
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

02:09.110 --> 02:14.650
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

02:14.650 --> 02:16.240
<i>baka darou?</i>

02:14.650 --> 02:16.240
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

02:16.240 --> 02:17.450
<i>ai</i>

02:16.240 --> 02:17.450
<i>Love!</i>

02:17.450 --> 02:20.950
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

02:17.450 --> 02:20.950
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

02:20.950 --> 02:30.840
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

02:20.950 --> 02:30.840
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

02:30.840 --> 02:31.670
<i>ai</i>

02:30.840 --> 02:31.670
<i>Love!</i>

02:31.670 --> 02:35.470
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

02:31.670 --> 02:35.470
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

02:35.470 --> 02:39.470
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

02:35.470 --> 02:39.470
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

02:39.470 --> 02:45.730
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

02:39.470 --> 02:45.730
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

02:45.730 --> 02:48.520
<i>hanasanai</i>

02:45.730 --> 02:48.520
<i>for a single moment!</i>

02:50.270 --> 02:54.770
<b><b>EPISODE 34: <b>
THE CURTAIN RAISES ON THE FIERCE BATTLE! <b>
THE TOURNAMENT STARTS!</b></b></b></b>

02:50.600 --> 02:52.580
Pass it over here!

02:52.580 --> 02:53.270
Run for it!

02:54.340 --> 02:57.370
I see, so you're living in France now.

02:57.370 --> 02:59.280
France is the land of the fine arts.

02:59.280 --> 03:02.380
If I remember correctly, your father was a painter.

03:02.380 --> 03:03.950
So you do remember.

03:04.800 --> 03:09.080
I still treasure the days I spent in Nankatsu with all of you.

03:09.670 --> 03:13.940
That ball is on display in my house in France,
as one of my prized possessions.

03:13.940 --> 03:16.490
Yeah, so is mine.

03:16.490 --> 03:17.700
Time sure flies.

03:17.700 --> 03:21.270
It's almost been 3 years since we parted ways with Tsubasa.

03:21.270 --> 03:23.240
But, you know, I was pretty shocked.

03:23.240 --> 03:25.560
You went ahead and came to visit me.

03:25.560 --> 03:31.670
Well, it's my summer holiday. Also, I've learned a bit of German.

03:31.670 --> 03:32.810
Is that so?

03:32.810 --> 03:37.990
Since you didn't contact us at all, I and the other guys from Nankatsu were worried.

03:37.990 --> 03:39.040
Sorry.

03:39.040 --> 03:41.740
I've been busy adapting to my new life in France.

03:41.740 --> 03:47.490
You know, I saw an article about you in a French football magazine.

03:47.490 --> 03:50.130
Is that what motivated you to come visit me?

03:50.130 --> 03:53.250
Yes. It looks like you're doing pretty well here!

03:53.250 --> 03:55.320
No, I'm still not there yet.

03:55.320 --> 03:58.790
And my "doing well" just means I'm on the B team.

03:58.790 --> 04:04.180
But, before I turn 18, I'll certainly make my debut in the pro league.

04:04.180 --> 04:06.260
You will. I expect a lot from you.

04:06.260 --> 04:12.240
By the way, Misaki, you <i>are</i> still playing football, aren't you?

04:12.240 --> 04:13.600
Of course!

04:14.900 --> 04:18.690
Just like how I kept playing wherever I went in Japan.

04:18.690 --> 04:23.800
Football is more popular in Europe than in Japan, particularly in France.

04:23.800 --> 04:26.140
No matter where I go, I can play football.

04:26.140 --> 04:27.150
So that's how it is?

04:27.150 --> 04:29.410
Hearing that puts my mind at ease.

04:29.410 --> 04:36.420
France's football is closer to the Latin style, where you can show your individual skills. You rarely see that in Europe.

04:36.420 --> 04:40.420
That should suit your artistic style.

04:40.420 --> 04:43.380
We have finally reunited, Misaki.

04:43.380 --> 04:45.150
How about going at it?

04:45.150 --> 04:48.180
Sure! Let's do it, Wakabayashi!

04:48.180 --> 04:49.020
Hey!

04:49.020 --> 04:50.680
Let us join, too!

04:56.260 --> 04:57.860
We can't take the ball...

04:58.580 --> 05:00.190
Misaki...

05:00.690 --> 05:05.320
<i>Tsubasa, Misaki is still great at controlling the ball.</i>

05:06.200 --> 05:07.660
<i>I've seen it myself. </i>

05:07.660 --> 05:09.120
All right, here I go!

05:10.760 --> 05:15.480
<i>Taro Misaki... He'll surely become a pro in the near future.</i>

05:15.480 --> 05:16.460
Oh...

05:17.250 --> 05:18.490
You're great!

05:18.490 --> 05:20.500
How can I get as good as you?

05:20.500 --> 05:25.640
Well... you can start by practicing.

05:25.640 --> 05:29.970
Do it 365 days a year; you should keep the ball with you at all times.

05:29.970 --> 05:31.970
The ball is your friend.

05:31.970 --> 05:36.980
A dear teammate I used to play with in Japan often said that.

05:40.670 --> 05:42.880
<i>Here is a picture from that day.</i>

05:42.880 --> 05:45.530
<i>I've also attached his address in France.</i>

05:45.530 --> 05:50.280
<i>Tsubasa, work hard to win that third consecutive national championship.</i>

05:50.820 --> 05:52.440
<i>Well, that's it for today.</i>

05:52.440 --> 05:53.500
<i>Regards, from Germany,</i>

05:53.500 --> 05:55.330
<i>Genzo Wakabayashi.</i>

05:55.330 --> 05:58.610
<i>I see... So Misaki was in France all along.</i>

05:58.610 --> 06:01.340
<i>That's why hasn't been in any Japanese tournaments.</i>

06:02.630 --> 06:04.810
<i>But... I'm really glad.</i>

06:04.810 --> 06:09.010
<i>Misaki is doing well, and he's still playing football.</i>

06:09.950 --> 06:11.930
<i>Wakabayashi is in Germany,</i>

06:11.930 --> 06:13.950
<i>and Misaki is in France. </i>

06:13.950 --> 06:18.170
<i>Now, it's my turn to go to Brazil and become a pro!</i>

06:18.170 --> 06:22.480
<i>Then together, we'll make Japanese football the greatest in the world.</i>

06:22.480 --> 06:26.150
<i>That is my real dream.</i>

06:26.150 --> 06:28.580
Okay Carlos, the time-out's over!

06:28.580 --> 06:29.640
Let's study!

06:29.640 --> 06:31.910
The match resumes, right?

06:31.910 --> 06:33.920
So what's the answer to that last question?

06:33.920 --> 06:35.710
It's a piece of cake for me!

06:37.580 --> 06:39.920
What? You're on the bullet train back?

06:39.920 --> 06:41.410
You're damn right, y'know!

06:41.410 --> 06:47.720
I was planning to stay over at your house for a bit and carefully do some recon on Nankatsu's practices

06:47.720 --> 06:48.920
but I've changed my mind.

06:48.920 --> 06:52.250
While I was watching Nankatsu's and Toho's final matches,

06:52.250 --> 06:54.930
it occurred to me that we can't rest on our laurels.

06:54.930 --> 06:57.240
We'll return to Nagasaki right away,

06:57.240 --> 07:00.080
and do train intensely until the tournament starts, y'know!

07:00.080 --> 07:03.100
Well, I kept perfect notes, you see.

07:03.100 --> 07:05.940
Yukari, pass this message to the guys at Nankatsu:

07:05.940 --> 07:12.700
At that Nationals, Hirado Middle School will stop them from getting their 3rd championship.

07:15.200 --> 07:17.200
this is the cutest TS in this episode

07:17.200 --> 07:19.090
Coach, it's me, Sawada.

07:19.090 --> 07:20.580
Come in.

07:20.580 --> 07:22.210
Coach, it's our captain.

07:22.210 --> 07:24.710
No matter where I look, I can't find Hyuga!

07:24.710 --> 07:26.500
What did you say?

07:32.060 --> 07:34.400
Lost the will to fight...

07:34.400 --> 07:36.430
A defanged tiger, huh?

07:40.690 --> 07:41.580
Whaaat?

07:41.580 --> 07:43.190
Misaki is in France?

07:43.190 --> 07:44.260
Here.

07:44.260 --> 07:45.190
Let me see...

07:46.030 --> 07:49.300
Wow, Misaki <i>is</i> in France!

07:50.320 --> 07:52.790
Wow, he's kind of hot...

07:52.790 --> 07:53.950
Who is this?

07:53.950 --> 07:57.690
He's Nankatsu SC's former player, Misaki.

07:57.690 --> 08:00.620
He and Tsubasa were called the Golden Duo.

08:00.620 --> 08:03.120
It was so awesome!

08:03.120 --> 08:04.610
I wouldn't have expected that.

08:04.610 --> 08:07.180
He looks like a very gentle person.

08:07.180 --> 08:10.960
But... <i>Tsubasa is still the best!</i>

08:10.960 --> 08:12.910
Oh, "but" what, Kumi?

08:12.910 --> 08:15.140
No-nothing!

08:15.140 --> 08:21.840
<i>Nankatsu Middle School, led by Tsubasa, is aiming for their 3rd championship for the first time in their school's history.</i>

08:21.840 --> 08:27.530
<i>Meanwhile, rivals from different cities are working to stop Nankatsu's 3rd consecutive victory at all costs.</i>

08:26.690 --> 08:30.360
HOKKAIDO - FURANO MIDDLE SCHOOL

08:27.530 --> 08:30.270
We'll take Nankatsu down this time!

08:30.270 --> 08:31.440
Yeah!

08:32.150 --> 08:33.100
We did it!

08:32.450 --> 08:36.490
AKITA - HANAWA MIDDLE SCHOOL

08:33.100 --> 08:34.430
We finally did it!

08:34.430 --> 08:36.550
This is our brand new combination play!

08:36.550 --> 08:39.030
Yeah, we finally did it, Masao!

08:39.080 --> 08:43.080
OSAKA - AZUMAICHI MIDDLE SCHOOL

08:39.710 --> 08:41.760
<i>And new challengers appear!</i>

08:41.760 --> 08:44.460
Our first entry will also be our first victory!

08:44.460 --> 08:46.210
What's wrong?

08:46.210 --> 08:49.210
We can't pretend we'll beat Nankatsu or Toho with just this, y'know!

08:46.290 --> 08:50.550
NAGASAKI - HIRADO MIDDLE SCHOOL

08:49.210 --> 08:50.490
Yeah!

08:50.490 --> 08:56.720
<i>As the Nationals draw near, each team keeps practicing, all fired up.</i>

08:57.460 --> 08:59.720
<i>As for Okinawa...</i>

08:59.720 --> 09:01.020
What's wrong?

09:01.020 --> 09:05.730
It's because you give up so easily that everyone says Japanese football's fallen behind!

09:05.730 --> 09:08.630
Use this sandy beach to strengthen your limbs.

09:08.630 --> 09:10.820
In football, it all comes down to your legs!

09:10.820 --> 09:11.730
Yes!

09:12.230 --> 09:13.610
Coach Kira...

09:13.610 --> 09:17.770
So you have come, Kojiro.

09:17.770 --> 09:18.540
Yes.

09:20.960 --> 09:22.370
What is the meaning of this?

09:22.370 --> 09:24.040
It's been a week already.

09:24.040 --> 09:27.330
What on earth is he thinking?

09:27.330 --> 09:28.500
Coach!

09:28.500 --> 09:32.440
I think our captain went to Okinawa, to Coach Kira.

09:32.440 --> 09:33.260
What did you say?

09:33.260 --> 09:34.680
Coach Kira?

09:34.680 --> 09:36.280
Who the hell is that?

09:36.280 --> 09:38.010
And did you just say Okinawa?

09:38.010 --> 09:39.810
Yes.

09:39.810 --> 09:43.020
Hyuga came here as a football scholarship student.

09:43.020 --> 09:44.780
Moreover, he's the captain.

09:44.780 --> 09:49.520
How can he act so selfishly when the Nationals should be his first and foremost priority?

09:49.520 --> 09:51.480
I will never condone such behavior!

09:51.480 --> 09:55.190
But I'm sure that he will return before the tournament.

09:55.190 --> 09:58.320
Enough! I'm fine if he never returns!

09:58.320 --> 10:03.080
In return, his right to a High School and University scholarship will be revoked!

10:03.080 --> 10:04.080
Wha—

10:04.080 --> 10:06.580
We'll play without him in the Nationals.

10:06.580 --> 10:07.940
Co—

10:07.940 --> 10:09.580
Coach!

10:10.130 --> 10:13.040
THE DAY BEFORE THE TOURNAMENT

10:13.040 --> 10:16.130
Whew, finally, some time to relax.

10:16.920 --> 10:20.970
Hey! As expected, we are considered the strongest contender to win it all.

10:20.970 --> 10:22.470
Let me see...

10:23.240 --> 10:26.160
Hey, there's a comment here from the Federation's Katagiri.

10:26.160 --> 10:27.000
Eh—

10:27.000 --> 10:33.480
He says that in his age group, there's probably no one able to beat the future ace of Japanese football, Tsubasa.

10:33.480 --> 10:37.700
Even for a Tsubasa fanboy, he sure exaggerates.

10:37.700 --> 10:41.160
If they see this, Hyuga and the others will get so mad.

10:43.020 --> 10:44.950
<i>You have no rivals.</i>

10:44.950 --> 10:47.830
<i>As things stand, that's my honest opinion.</i>

10:48.760 --> 10:52.910
<i>However, Tsubasa, this will also put pressure on you.</i>

10:52.910 --> 10:59.340
<i>It means that I hope a rival strong enough to defeat you will appear in Japan.</i>

11:00.580 --> 11:03.640
<i>Mr. Katagiri, even if you say that, I won't lose.</i>

11:03.640 --> 11:09.240
<i>If I can't become #1 in Japan, even if I go to the kingdom of football, Brazil, it will be in vain.</i>

11:09.240 --> 11:10.760
What the hell is that?

11:11.350 --> 11:13.910
What's gotten hold of you so suddenly, Ishizaki?

11:13.910 --> 11:15.110
Just look at this.

11:15.110 --> 11:18.110
NEWS-INFO
Captain of Toho Academy, Kojiro Hyuga, has mysteriously disappeared! Coach Kitazume says "We'll play without Hyuga"...

11:15.110 --> 11:18.110
It looks like this just got in. It's quite brief, but...

11:18.110 --> 11:20.020
Th-this...

11:20.020 --> 11:21.740
Hyuga has disappeared!

11:21.740 --> 11:22.980
Wha—

11:33.820 --> 11:38.130
<i>Number 7, the large-scale typhoon,
is about to reach the main island of Okinawa.</i>

11:38.130 --> 11:42.860
<i>There will be tall waves at the coastal area; caution is advised.</i>

11:38.130 --> 11:42.860
stop it, wave kun you can't surf with a ball, ko-chan

11:56.070 --> 11:57.480
Go!

12:06.820 --> 12:09.200
Damn...!

12:09.200 --> 12:14.960
Look at that, that city boy from Tokyo
is still practicing, despite the huge waves.

12:14.960 --> 12:16.920
Shouldn't we go out to stop him?

12:16.920 --> 12:18.920
It's not like it's just today...

12:18.920 --> 12:22.790
Apparently, Coach Kira made him work hard until midnight, yesterday.

12:22.790 --> 12:24.430
Get your ass up, Kojiro!

12:24.430 --> 12:27.180
It's enough to give you chills...

12:28.100 --> 12:31.980
Does one really need to work on football this hard...?

12:37.160 --> 12:38.190
<i>Kojiro.</i>

12:43.510 --> 12:44.530
<i>I...</i>

12:45.440 --> 12:46.760
<i>I am...</i>

12:49.030 --> 12:50.970
<i>...sick of losing, every time...!</i>

12:52.040 --> 12:58.960
<i>I'm sick of losing... to Tsubasa Ozora!</i>

13:02.470 --> 13:06.970
<i>Explosive kicking power, strong enough to pierce through the raging waves...</i>

13:06.970 --> 13:13.480
<i>Moreover, enough lower body strength to allow him to stand without flinching against the waves...</i>

13:13.480 --> 13:16.230
<i>Were you able to pull it off finally, Kojiro?</i>

13:21.230 --> 13:24.140
<i>That scorching fighting spirit of yours...</i>

13:24.140 --> 13:26.240
<i>The tiger who refound his fangs,</i>

13:27.490 --> 13:32.400
<i>is back from his slumber now!</i>

13:35.500 --> 13:39.000
THE DAY OF THE TOURNAMENT

13:36.180 --> 13:39.000
<i>And finally, it is the day of the tournament.</i>

13:39.000 --> 13:40.620
Hurry up and get in, boys!

13:40.620 --> 13:42.010
We are heading off.

13:42.010 --> 13:43.510
Y-Yes sir!

13:43.510 --> 13:45.020
It can't be...

13:45.020 --> 13:47.540
Hyuga didn't come back after all.

13:47.540 --> 13:50.260
Are we really going to fight without Captain?

13:57.410 --> 13:58.270
Kojiro.

13:59.640 --> 14:00.810
Kojiro!

14:04.750 --> 14:06.900
Wake up, Kojiro!

14:08.340 --> 14:10.410
Coach Kira.

14:11.040 --> 14:13.910
You did well to endure this entire week.

14:16.910 --> 14:19.670
Here's an airplane ticket to Tokyo.

14:19.670 --> 14:23.420
Go now, Kojiro, and go wild out there!

14:24.620 --> 14:26.170
Sure!

14:27.360 --> 14:28.340
Hurry up.

14:28.340 --> 14:30.550
If we don't, Nankatsu will have left their inn.

14:30.550 --> 14:34.040
We need to get a comment from Tsubasa at all costs before that happens.

14:34.040 --> 14:35.060
Yes sir.

14:36.060 --> 14:37.000
Whoa!

14:37.000 --> 14:38.670
Sir, that's...

14:39.970 --> 14:41.180
Tsubasa!

14:41.180 --> 14:42.360
What is he doing there?

14:49.660 --> 14:51.030
What?!

14:51.030 --> 14:52.410
Don't tell me that shot was...

14:53.990 --> 14:55.790
Still not good, huh?

14:56.650 --> 15:00.730
<i>"Tsubasa, fire your long shots with a drive effect on them."</i>

15:00.730 --> 15:04.250
<i>Unless you master that shot, you won't be able to become a first-class player.</i>

15:04.250 --> 15:08.510
<i>The shot takes a sharp dive after flying in from up high, getting over the keeper.</i>

15:08.510 --> 15:15.260
<i>Tsubasa, this is a Brazilian level... No, it is a world-class shot...</i>

15:15.970 --> 15:19.940
<i>Roberto, I will win this tournament for sure.</i>

15:20.580 --> 15:21.950
<i>And then...</i>

15:26.940 --> 15:29.200
<i>It's about time for the opening ceremony.</i>

15:29.200 --> 15:31.950
<i>It appears Okinawa suffered a typhoon yesterday,</i>

15:31.950 --> 15:34.300
<i>but here in Saitama we have a clear weather!</i>

15:34.300 --> 15:37.450
<i>The scorching sun of August is shining upon the ground.</i>

15:38.240 --> 15:42.290
<i>The first ones to enter are Shizuoka's representatives, Nankatsu MS,</i>

15:42.290 --> 15:47.960
<i>who are the center of attention, the focus being on whether they'll get their first-in-history 3rd win in a row.</i>

15:47.960 --> 15:51.090
FURANO MIDDLE SCHOOL
HOKKAIDO

15:47.960 --> 15:51.840
<i>46 other representatives from all around Japan have made their way onto this stage,</i>

15:51.840 --> 15:53.840
<i>and are appearing one by one after them.</i>

15:54.720 --> 15:57.170
<i>The competition will follow an elimination format.</i>

15:57.170 --> 15:59.850
<i>One loss will be enough to drop out.</i>

15:59.850 --> 16:06.770
<i>Aren't they all aiming for the same thing, the crimson colored championship pennant?</i>

16:06.770 --> 16:08.890
We will take it this year.

16:08.890 --> 16:10.280
But of course!

16:10.280 --> 16:11.780
Hmph.

16:11.780 --> 16:14.530
No need for a hassle, it will be ours anyway, y'know.

16:14.530 --> 16:17.930
We will return to Hokkaido with that pennant this year!

16:17.930 --> 16:19.030
Am I right, guys?

16:19.030 --> 16:20.040
Yeah!

16:20.540 --> 16:22.270
<i>I won't give it to anyone.</i>

16:22.270 --> 16:25.140
<i>I will have that championship pennant in my hands</i>

16:25.140 --> 16:27.040
<i>once again, on the final day of tournament!</i>

16:27.040 --> 16:29.100
Hey, look at that.

16:30.420 --> 16:33.720
See, Hyuga is really missing from Toho's roster.

16:33.720 --> 16:35.510
Yeah, you're right.

16:36.520 --> 16:37.800
Sanae.

16:39.620 --> 16:40.720
Long time no see.

16:40.720 --> 16:42.190
Yayoi!

16:42.190 --> 16:43.230
Jun, come here!

16:43.860 --> 16:45.350
Jun?

16:45.350 --> 16:47.400
Hey, it's been a while.

16:47.400 --> 16:48.980
Misugi!

16:48.980 --> 16:49.860
Ba-dump!

16:51.360 --> 16:54.010
Yukari, get a hold of yourself!

16:55.770 --> 16:57.740
So, it's "Jun" instead of "Captain" now, I see.

16:57.740 --> 17:00.600
What are you saying, Sanae...!

17:00.600 --> 17:04.760
By the way, the Tokyo tournament was close, wasn't it, Misugi?

17:07.380 --> 17:10.130
That was the best of me, though.

17:10.130 --> 17:12.490
<i>Now that the opening ceremony is over,</i>

17:12.490 --> 17:14.490
<i>the first match will begin immediately.</i>

17:14.490 --> 17:17.840
<i>The match will be between last year's champions, Nankatsu MS,</i>

17:17.840 --> 17:20.190
<i>against first time contenders Azumaichi MS, from Osaka.</i>

17:20.190 --> 17:25.760
<i>This, along with the match between Toho Academy and Matsukami MS, will be the only matches today.</i>

17:25.760 --> 17:29.730
<i>As a result, most of the participating teams will be watching from the stands.</i>

17:29.730 --> 17:32.480
All right then, let's see what you've got.

17:32.480 --> 17:35.740
I wonder what kind of football will Nankatsu display.

17:36.400 --> 17:37.340
Mr. Mikami.

17:37.340 --> 17:38.160
Hmm?

17:38.160 --> 17:40.490
Hello there, Katagiri.

17:40.490 --> 17:42.450
Are you here to observe Nankatsu after all?

17:42.450 --> 17:44.480
Yeah, you could say that.

17:44.480 --> 17:49.460
But... this generation is said to be on a
higher level one than any one before it.

17:49.460 --> 17:54.480
You never know when and where
a great player may show themselves.

17:54.480 --> 17:59.320
That premonition of yours might become real, right at this first game.

18:00.750 --> 18:04.110
Lady luck isn't smiling on us with this bracket.

18:04.110 --> 18:07.310
Hanawa and the Tachibana Twins are right beside us.

18:07.310 --> 18:10.660
Furano is also in the next block.

18:10.660 --> 18:15.240
If things go as usual, our opponents will be tough, right up to the final match against Toho.

18:15.240 --> 18:17.740
It doesn't matter who we get matched with.

18:17.740 --> 18:20.740
This will be our last tournament as 3rd years.

18:20.740 --> 18:22.950
Like hell we'd let anyone beat us, even once!

18:24.900 --> 18:25.870
Manabu.

18:26.460 --> 18:29.420
I hear our first opponent, Azumaichi,

18:29.420 --> 18:31.680
is participating for the first time.

18:31.680 --> 18:35.550
They're the team that defeated Naniwa, where Nakanishi was at, right?

18:35.550 --> 18:37.050
Yeah.

18:37.050 --> 18:39.100
A quick offense right after a tight defense;

18:39.100 --> 18:43.280
it seems they used counter attacks
to win their way through the Osaka regionals.

18:43.280 --> 18:48.620
Azumaichi has a rather unique trait, too.

18:49.190 --> 18:51.460
It's their top scorer.

18:51.460 --> 18:54.420
He is not a forward—he's actually a defender.

18:54.420 --> 18:55.440
Huh?!

18:55.440 --> 18:59.400
#7, Makoto Soda, playing the center back position.

18:59.400 --> 19:05.280
He is the core of their defense, and on top of that, he's scored nearly all of their goals.

19:06.040 --> 19:07.990
Center back, huh?

19:07.990 --> 19:09.030
<i>That's</i> interesting.

19:09.030 --> 19:10.740
It's got me all fired up!

19:10.740 --> 19:16.450
If that's the case, how about you go for the first goal in the tournament?

19:16.450 --> 19:18.920
Hell yeah, I am up for it!

19:18.920 --> 19:21.330
{le bruh sound}I... was joking, though.

19:22.930 --> 19:24.860
Boys, the match is about to start.

19:24.860 --> 19:27.020
Go out there and warm up!

19:27.020 --> 19:28.270
Yes, sir!

19:28.270 --> 19:30.270
AZUMAICHI MIDDLE SCHOOL
OSAKA

19:29.520 --> 19:30.270
Listen to me!

19:30.270 --> 19:33.780
At the end of the day, Nankatsu is all about Tsubasa Ozora!

19:33.780 --> 19:36.930
As long as we can keep him held down, we can win this!

19:36.930 --> 19:37.960
Yes, sir!

19:37.960 --> 19:42.090
Soda, you will be marking him. I expect you to do it perfectly.

19:42.090 --> 19:43.660
Please, just leave it to me.

19:43.660 --> 19:47.680
Just the thought of defeating Tsubasa Ozora
in front of such an large audience

19:47.680 --> 19:49.940
makes me so happy that I can't contain myself.

19:49.940 --> 19:53.920
I will show them my sharpness with all its edge.

19:54.940 --> 19:58.960
<i>On the other side, Toho Academy arrived at the Bay Coast Stadium</i>

19:58.960 --> 20:01.970
<i>where the other match will be held.</i>

20:02.660 --> 20:05.260
Our match will start 90 minutes later.

20:05.260 --> 20:08.050
Make sure you get enough rest until then.

20:08.050 --> 20:09.470
Yes, sir!

20:09.880 --> 20:10.480
Huh?

20:10.480 --> 20:11.270
Oh!

20:13.350 --> 20:15.540
Captain!

20:15.540 --> 20:16.480
Hyuga!

20:17.760 --> 20:21.990
Coach, I've just returned from Okinawa.

20:26.460 --> 20:29.880
Hyuga, I won't allow you to play in this tournament.

20:32.000 --> 20:33.340
C-Coach!

20:33.340 --> 20:34.250
Hyuga!

20:42.760 --> 20:44.460
Hurry up!

20:47.160 --> 20:49.140
It seems we were in time!

20:49.140 --> 20:52.640
Go! Clamp them hard, clamp them hard! 'ichi Middle!

20:52.930 --> 20:56.190
Hooray! Hooray! Nankatsu!

20:56.190 --> 20:57.990
Ishizaki!

20:58.690 --> 21:00.980
We came here to support you guys, as promised!

21:00.980 --> 21:02.580
Oh, it's Urabe and his guys!

21:02.580 --> 21:05.930
You are Shizuoka's representatives, who defeated us!

21:05.930 --> 21:07.570
Make sure you become champions!

21:07.570 --> 21:09.570
Otherwise, I won't have mercy!

21:09.570 --> 21:11.100
Sure, count on us!

21:11.100 --> 21:14.040
Hey, can you stop getting ahead of yourselves and hurry the hell up?

21:14.040 --> 21:14.580
What did...?!

21:14.970 --> 21:18.170
Don't get too comfortable, just because you've won twice.

21:18.170 --> 21:19.870
Say that again you jerk!

21:19.870 --> 21:20.750
Ishizaki.

21:22.700 --> 21:24.850
So, you are <i>the</i> Tsubasa Ozora.

21:24.850 --> 21:27.680
You don't even look that big up close.

21:27.680 --> 21:30.060
I will be marking you, so let's be nice to each other.

21:30.060 --> 21:33.060
You there, stop talking like that.

21:33.060 --> 21:36.810
Even if it's before the match, if you keep this up, I'll eject you.

21:36.810 --> 21:38.200
Get in the line!

21:38.200 --> 21:40.320
Yeah, sure, got it.

21:41.740 --> 21:44.820
That's Makoto Soda.

21:44.820 --> 21:48.540
<i>Nankatsu gets the ball with the coin toss.</i>

21:48.540 --> 21:52.160
<i>The players from both teams get into formation.</i>

21:52.160 --> 21:54.290
<i>Let's start with this first match now.</i>

21:54.290 --> 21:56.540
<i>We will be the champions once again!</i>

21:56.540 --> 21:58.290
<i>It's V3! </i>

21:58.290 --> 21:59.540
<i>I will protect!</i>

21:59.540 --> 22:01.130
<i>I will attack!</i>

22:01.130 --> 22:06.880
<i>The hugely anticipated first game... starts now!</i>

22:08.800 --> 22:10.000
Fools.

22:10.000 --> 22:13.130
There won't be a V3 for you!

22:38.830 --> 22:44.880
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.830 --> 22:44.880
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.880 --> 22:50.890
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.880 --> 22:50.890
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.890 --> 22:56.930
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.890 --> 22:56.930
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.930 --> 23:01.560
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.930 --> 23:01.560
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.190 --> 23:07.860
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.190 --> 23:07.860
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.200 --> 23:15.290
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.200 --> 23:15.290
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.290 --> 23:21.330
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.330 --> 23:25.800
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.330 --> 23:25.800
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.090 --> 23:33.430
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.090 --> 23:33.430
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.430 --> 23:39.480
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.480 --> 23:45.770
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.480 --> 23:45.770
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.110 --> 24:00.740
COMING UP, EPISODE 35:
RAZOR POWER EXPLODES
